window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b250-918c6319ffd3a264.json"]={sha256:"918c6319ffd3a2645f035435cb1d7f2be65bfa6ca23ec652c2a2bb0e16d2762a",value:{"id":"b250","title":"大型弧形閘門安裝","titleEn":"Large radial-gate installation","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課以以鉸軸幾何受力傳遞與同步試運轉安裝弧門為主線，先用曲面水壓與水平力與曲面垂直分量界定水力與構造條件，再將吊索角度與張力、支臂長細與屈曲連結到同步行程與試運轉。算例為準靜態簡化構件，起吊與蓄水驗收仍須核准吊裝計畫、結構分析及現場量測。 每單元以原創算例、量測與失效辨識共同檢查推論。","summaryEn":"This course develops installing radial gates through trunnion geometry load paths and synchronized commissioning through Curved pressure and horizontal force and Vertical pressure component, then connects Sling angle and tension and Arm slenderness and buckling to Synchronized travel and commissioning. Examples idealize quasi-static components; lifting and impoundment acceptance require approved plans structural analysis and field measurements. Each unit combines original calculation, measurement and failure diagnosis to test the inference.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-hydraulics","subcategoryTitle":"壩工監測、溢洪與壓力水路","subcategoryTitleEn":"Dam monitoring, spillways and pressure waterways","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-hydraulics","learningTags":["water","water-hydraulics","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-hydraulic","architectureNodes":[["曲面水壓與水平力","Curved pressure and horizontal force"],["雙鉸軸同軸量測","Trunnion coaxiality surveying"],["吊索角度與張力","Sling angle and tension"],["支臂長細與屈曲","Arm slenderness and buckling"],["同步行程與試運轉","Synchronized travel and commissioning"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[0,3]],"diagram":{"type":"water-hydraulic","labels":["曲面水壓與水平力","雙鉸軸同軸量測","吊索角度與張力","支臂長細與屈曲","同步行程與試運轉"],"labelsEn":["Curved pressure and horizontal force","Trunnion coaxiality surveying","Sling angle and tension","Arm slenderness and buckling","Synchronized travel and commissioning"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"整合算例輸入全為教學假設，先檢查曲面水壓與水平力：Vertical rectangular projection from free surface: width=8 m; depth=6 m; horizontalForce=0.5*9.81*8*6**2=1412.64 kN；再獨立檢查曲面垂直分量：Specified imaginary waterVolume=45 m3; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; verticalMagnitude=45*9.81=441.45 kN; direction from free body。敏感度：相同矩形投影寬度8m下，水深由6增至7m時水平靜水力由1412.64增至1922.76kN，增加36.11%；荷載按水深平方成長，不能用水位增加百分比直接放大全部構件反力。 兩個結果須按各自量綱解釋，不能直接相加或當成完整設計。算例為準靜態簡化構件，起吊與蓄水驗收仍須核准吊裝計畫、結構分析及現場量測。 將核對預緊紀錄灌漿完整性與支座變形再比較分載作為獨立驗證，明確列出尚缺的現地輸入及其對結論的影響。","textEn":"Every input in this integrated example is a teaching assumption. First examine Curved pressure and horizontal force: Vertical rectangular projection from free surface: width=8 m; depth=6 m; horizontalForce=0.5*9.81*8*6**2=1412.64 kN. Independently examine Vertical pressure component: Specified imaginary waterVolume=45 m3; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; verticalMagnitude=45*9.81=441.45 kN; direction from free body. Sensitivity: for an8m-wide rectangular projection, raising depth from6 to7m increases horizontal hydrostatic force from1412.64 to1922.76kN, or36.11 percent. This quadratic change does not imply the same factor for every component reaction. Interpret each result in its own dimensions rather than adding them or treating them as a complete design. Examples idealize quasi-static components; lifting and impoundment acceptance require approved plans structural analysis and field measurements. Use the following independent check: Review preload, grout continuity and support deformation before comparing load sharing. Identify missing field inputs and state which conclusions depend on them.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b250-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「曲面水壓與水平力」與「曲面垂直分量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Curved pressure and horizontal force\" and \"Vertical pressure component\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b250-v15-01","title":"曲面水壓與水平力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Curved pressure and horizontal force: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「曲面水壓與水平力」如何影響大型弧形閘門安裝的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Curved pressure and horizontal force” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Large radial-gate installation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"弧門曲面上的靜水壓沿表面法線作用，理想同心圓弧的壓力線通過鉸軸，但合力仍須分解成水平與垂直分量。水平分量可用垂直投影面計算；此便利不表示閘門沒有重量、摩擦或偏心力矩，安裝幾何與受力必須共同核對。 驗證時應核對水位與曲面垂直投影尺寸並確認鉸軸位置，並辨識以下失效情境：圓弧中心偏離鉸軸會增加原本理想模型沒有的水壓力矩。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「曲面水壓與水平力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Hydrostatic pressure acts normal to the curved skin, and ideal concentric normals pass through the trunnion. Resolve the resultant into horizontal and vertical components. The horizontal component follows the vertical projection, but weight, friction and eccentricity still create moments that depend on installed geometry. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Check water level and projected dimensions and survey the trunnion position. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: A curvature center offset from the trunnion adds hydrostatic moment absent from the ideal model. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Curved pressure and horizontal force” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Vertical rectangular projection from free surface: width=8 m; depth=6 m; horizontalForce=0.5*9.81*8*6**2=1412.64 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Vertical rectangular projection from free surface: width=8 m; depth=6 m; horizontalForce=0.5*9.81*8*6**2=1412.64 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「理想弧門水壓通過鉸軸就代表全部荷載皆無力矩」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Pressure passing through the trunnion means every gate load has zero moment\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「曲面水壓與水平力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Curved pressure and horizontal force”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-01-k1","title":"曲面水壓與水平力","titleEn":"Curved pressure and horizontal force","text":"弧門曲面上的靜水壓沿表面法線作用，理想同心圓弧的壓力線通過鉸軸，但合力仍須分解成水平與垂直分量。水平分量可用垂直投影面計算；此便利不表示閘門沒有重量、摩擦或偏心力矩，安裝幾何與受力必須共同核對。","textEn":"Hydrostatic pressure acts normal to the curved skin, and ideal concentric normals pass through the trunnion. Resolve the resultant into horizontal and vertical components.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：理想弧門水壓通過鉸軸就代表全部荷載皆無力矩 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Pressure passing through the trunnion means every gate load has zero moment Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「曲面水壓與水平力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Curved pressure and horizontal force\" is correct?","options":["理想弧門水壓通過鉸軸就代表全部荷載皆無力矩","弧門曲面上的靜水壓沿表面法線作用，理想同心圓弧的壓力線通過鉸軸，但合力仍須分解成水平與垂直分量。","曲面面積乘平均壓力必然就是垂直水壓力"],"optionsEn":["Pressure passing through the trunnion means every gate load has zero moment","Hydrostatic pressure acts normal to the curved skin, and ideal concentric normals pass through the trunnion.","Curved area times mean pressure always equals vertical hydrostatic force"],"answer":1,"explanation":"弧門曲面上的靜水壓沿表面法線作用，理想同心圓弧的壓力線通過鉸軸，但合力仍須分解成水平與垂直分量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Hydrostatic pressure acts normal to the curved skin, and ideal concentric normals pass through the trunnion. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b250-v15-02","title":"曲面水壓與水平力：定量估算","titleEn":"Curved pressure and horizontal force: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「曲面水壓與水平力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Curved pressure and horizontal force” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Vertical rectangular projection from free surface: width=8 m; depth=6 m; horizontalForce=0.5*9.81*8*6**2=1412.64 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Vertical rectangular projection from free surface: width=8 m; depth=6 m; horizontalForce=0.5*9.81*8*6**2=1412.64 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對水位與曲面垂直投影尺寸並確認鉸軸位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check water level and projected dimensions and survey the trunnion position.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Vertical rectangular projection from free surface: width=8 m; depth=6 m; horizontalForce=0.5*9.81*8*6**2=1412.64 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Vertical rectangular projection from free surface: width=8 m; depth=6 m; horizontalForce=0.5*9.81*8*6**2=1412.64 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「曲面水壓與水平力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Curved pressure and horizontal force\", which statement holds?","options":["軸承反力不變就表示摩擦力矩永遠不變","面板總面積相同就保證局部彎曲完全相同","原創教學假設：Vertical rectangular projection from free surface: width=8 m; depth=6 m; horizontalForce=0.5*9.81*8*6**2=1412.64 kN。"],"optionsEn":["Constant bearing reaction guarantees constant friction torque","Equal total skin area guarantees identical local bending","Original teaching assumptions: Vertical rectangular projection from free surface: width=8 m; depth=6 m; horizontalForce=0.5*9.81*8*6**2=1412.64 kN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Vertical rectangular projection from free surface: width=8 m; depth=6 m; horizontalForce=0.5*9.81*8*6**2=1412.64 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Vertical rectangular projection from free surface: width=8 m; depth=6 m; horizontalForce=0.5*9.81*8*6**2=1412.64 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b250-v15-03","title":"曲面水壓與水平力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Curved pressure and horizontal force: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「曲面水壓與水平力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Curved pressure and horizontal force” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對水位與曲面垂直投影尺寸並確認鉸軸位置。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「圓弧中心偏離鉸軸會增加原本理想模型沒有的水壓力矩」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check water level and projected dimensions and survey the trunnion position. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A curvature center offset from the trunnion adds hydrostatic moment absent from the ideal model. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以核對水位與曲面垂直投影尺寸並確認鉸軸位置作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對圓弧中心偏離鉸軸會增加原本理想模型沒有的水壓力矩，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check water level and projected dimensions and survey the trunnion position. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A curvature center offset from the trunnion adds hydrostatic moment absent from the ideal model. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：圓弧中心偏離鉸軸會增加原本理想模型沒有的水壓力矩。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A curvature center offset from the trunnion adds hydrostatic moment absent from the ideal model. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對水位與曲面垂直投影尺寸並確認鉸軸位置。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「圓弧中心偏離鉸軸會增加原本理想模型沒有的水壓力矩」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Check water level and projected dimensions and survey the trunnion position. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A curvature center offset from the trunnion adds hydrostatic moment absent from the ideal model. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以核對水位與曲面垂直投影尺寸並確認鉸軸位置作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對圓弧中心偏離鉸軸會增加原本理想模型沒有的水壓力矩，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check water level and projected dimensions and survey the trunnion position. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A curvature center offset from the trunnion adds hydrostatic moment absent from the ideal model. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「曲面水壓與水平力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Curved pressure and horizontal force\"?","options":["核對水位與曲面垂直投影尺寸並確認鉸軸位置。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","總拉力除錨栓數就是每支錨栓的實際最大力"],"optionsEn":["Check water level and projected dimensions and survey the trunnion position.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Total tension divided by anchor count equals every anchor maximum"],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對水位與曲面垂直投影尺寸並確認鉸軸位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check water level and projected dimensions and survey the trunnion position. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b250-v15-04","title":"曲面水壓與水平力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Curved pressure and horizontal force: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「曲面水壓與水平力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Curved pressure and horizontal force” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"圓弧中心偏離鉸軸會增加原本理想模型沒有的水壓力矩。診斷時應採取以下查核：核對水位與曲面垂直投影尺寸並確認鉸軸位置，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A curvature center offset from the trunnion adds hydrostatic moment absent from the ideal model. Diagnose it by the following check: Check water level and projected dimensions and survey the trunnion position. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「理想弧門水壓通過鉸軸就代表全部荷載皆無力矩」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Pressure passing through the trunnion means every gate load has zero moment\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"圓弧中心偏離鉸軸會增加原本理想模型沒有的水壓力矩。診斷時應採取以下查核：核對水位與曲面垂直投影尺寸並確認鉸軸位置，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"A curvature center offset from the trunnion adds hydrostatic moment absent from the ideal model. Diagnose it by the following check: Check water level and projected dimensions and survey the trunnion position. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「曲面水壓與水平力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Curved pressure and horizontal force\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","圓弧中心偏離鉸軸會增加原本理想模型沒有的水壓力矩。","曲面面積乘平均壓力必然就是垂直水壓力"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A curvature center offset from the trunnion adds hydrostatic moment absent from the ideal model.","Curved area times mean pressure always equals vertical hydrostatic force"],"answer":1,"explanation":"圓弧中心偏離鉸軸會增加原本理想模型沒有的水壓力矩。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A curvature center offset from the trunnion adds hydrostatic moment absent from the ideal model. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b250-v15-05","title":"曲面垂直分量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Vertical pressure component: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「曲面垂直分量」如何影響大型弧形閘門安裝的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Vertical pressure component” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Large radial-gate installation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"曲面靜水力的垂直分量可由相應虛擬水體重量求得，方向取決於受壓面朝向與邊界。必須在自由體圖明示選用哪一水體，不能把曲面面積乘平均壓力當垂直力；此分量還會改變鉸支承反力與啟閉需求。 驗證時應以剖面圖圈選虛擬水體並與壓力向量積分交叉比較，並辨識以下失效情境：選錯虛擬水體或方向會錯估鉸支承垂直反力。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「曲面垂直分量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The vertical hydrostatic component corresponds to an appropriate imaginary water volume, with direction set by surface orientation. Show that volume explicitly in the free-body diagram; curved area times average pressure is not automatically a vertical force. This component also affects bearing reaction and operating demand. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Mark the imaginary volume on a section and compare it with pressure-vector integration. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Choosing the wrong volume or direction misstates vertical trunnion reaction. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Vertical pressure component” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Specified imaginary waterVolume=45 m3; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; verticalMagnitude=45*9.81=441.45 kN; direction from free body。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Specified imaginary waterVolume=45 m3; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; verticalMagnitude=45*9.81=441.45 kN; direction from free body.","failure":"常見誤解：「曲面面積乘平均壓力必然就是垂直水壓力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Curved area times mean pressure always equals vertical hydrostatic force\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「曲面垂直分量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Vertical pressure component”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-05-k1","title":"曲面垂直分量","titleEn":"Vertical pressure component","text":"曲面靜水力的垂直分量可由相應虛擬水體重量求得，方向取決於受壓面朝向與邊界。必須在自由體圖明示選用哪一水體，不能把曲面面積乘平均壓力當垂直力；此分量還會改變鉸支承反力與啟閉需求。","textEn":"The vertical hydrostatic component corresponds to an appropriate imaginary water volume, with direction set by surface orientation. Show that volume explicitly in the free-body diagram; curved area times average pressure is not automatically a vertical force.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：曲面面積乘平均壓力必然就是垂直水壓力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Curved area times mean pressure always equals vertical hydrostatic force Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「曲面垂直分量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Vertical pressure component\" is correct?","options":["曲面面積乘平均壓力必然就是垂直水壓力","兩鉸中心同高就保證三維軸線完全同軸","曲面靜水力的垂直分量可由相應虛擬水體重量求得，方向取決於受壓面朝向與邊界。"],"optionsEn":["Curved area times mean pressure always equals vertical hydrostatic force","Equal trunnion-center elevations guarantee complete three-dimensional coaxiality","The vertical hydrostatic component corresponds to an appropriate imaginary water volume, with direction set by surface orientation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"曲面靜水力的垂直分量可由相應虛擬水體重量求得，方向取決於受壓面朝向與邊界。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The vertical hydrostatic component corresponds to an appropriate imaginary water volume, with direction set by surface orientation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b250-v15-06","title":"曲面垂直分量：定量估算","titleEn":"Vertical pressure component: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「曲面垂直分量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Vertical pressure component” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Specified imaginary waterVolume=45 m3; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; verticalMagnitude=45*9.81=441.45 kN; direction from free body。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Specified imaginary waterVolume=45 m3; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; verticalMagnitude=45*9.81=441.45 kN; direction from free body. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以剖面圖圈選虛擬水體並與壓力向量積分交叉比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mark the imaginary volume on a section and compare it with pressure-vector integration.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Specified imaginary waterVolume=45 m3; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; verticalMagnitude=45*9.81=441.45 kN; direction from free body。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Specified imaginary waterVolume=45 m3; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; verticalMagnitude=45*9.81=441.45 kN; direction from free body. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「曲面垂直分量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Vertical pressure component\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：Specified imaginary waterVolume=45 m3; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; verticalMagnitude=45*9.81=441.45 kN; direction from free body。","兩根吊索不論角度都各承受總重的一半","理想歐拉屈曲力就是現場支臂可直接承受荷載"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: Specified imaginary waterVolume=45 m3; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; verticalMagnitude=45*9.81=441.45 kN; direction from free body.","Two slings each carry half the weight regardless of angle","Ideal Euler load is the directly usable field capacity of the arm"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Specified imaginary waterVolume=45 m3; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; verticalMagnitude=45*9.81=441.45 kN; direction from free body。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Specified imaginary waterVolume=45 m3; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; verticalMagnitude=45*9.81=441.45 kN; direction from free body. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b250-v15-07","title":"曲面垂直分量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Vertical pressure component: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「曲面垂直分量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Vertical pressure component” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以剖面圖圈選虛擬水體並與壓力向量積分交叉比較。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「選錯虛擬水體或方向會錯估鉸支承垂直反力」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mark the imaginary volume on a section and compare it with pressure-vector integration. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Choosing the wrong volume or direction misstates vertical trunnion reaction. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以剖面圖圈選虛擬水體並與壓力向量積分交叉比較作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對選錯虛擬水體或方向會錯估鉸支承垂直反力，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Mark the imaginary volume on a section and compare it with pressure-vector integration. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Choosing the wrong volume or direction misstates vertical trunnion reaction. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：選錯虛擬水體或方向會錯估鉸支承垂直反力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Choosing the wrong volume or direction misstates vertical trunnion reaction. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以剖面圖圈選虛擬水體並與壓力向量積分交叉比較。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「選錯虛擬水體或方向會錯估鉸支承垂直反力」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Mark the imaginary volume on a section and compare it with pressure-vector integration. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Choosing the wrong volume or direction misstates vertical trunnion reaction. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以剖面圖圈選虛擬水體並與壓力向量積分交叉比較作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對選錯虛擬水體或方向會錯估鉸支承垂直反力，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Mark the imaginary volume on a section and compare it with pressure-vector integration. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Choosing the wrong volume or direction misstates vertical trunnion reaction. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「曲面垂直分量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Vertical pressure component\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以剖面圖圈選虛擬水體並與壓力向量積分交叉比較。","止水壓縮越多就必定越好且沒有代價"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Mark the imaginary volume on a section and compare it with pressure-vector integration.","More seal compression is always better and has no adverse effect"],"answer":1,"explanation":"以剖面圖圈選虛擬水體並與壓力向量積分交叉比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mark the imaginary volume on a section and compare it with pressure-vector integration. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b250-v15-08","title":"曲面垂直分量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Vertical pressure component: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「曲面垂直分量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Vertical pressure component” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"選錯虛擬水體或方向會錯估鉸支承垂直反力。診斷時應採取以下查核：以剖面圖圈選虛擬水體並與壓力向量積分交叉比較，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Choosing the wrong volume or direction misstates vertical trunnion reaction. Diagnose it by the following check: Mark the imaginary volume on a section and compare it with pressure-vector integration. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「曲面面積乘平均壓力必然就是垂直水壓力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Curved area times mean pressure always equals vertical hydrostatic force\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"選錯虛擬水體或方向會錯估鉸支承垂直反力。診斷時應採取以下查核：以剖面圖圈選虛擬水體並與壓力向量積分交叉比較，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Choosing the wrong volume or direction misstates vertical trunnion reaction. Diagnose it by the following check: Mark the imaginary volume on a section and compare it with pressure-vector integration. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「曲面垂直分量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Vertical pressure component\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","兩鉸中心同高就保證三維軸線完全同軸","選錯虛擬水體或方向會錯估鉸支承垂直反力。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Equal trunnion-center elevations guarantee complete three-dimensional coaxiality","Choosing the wrong volume or direction misstates vertical trunnion reaction."],"answer":2,"explanation":"選錯虛擬水體或方向會錯估鉸支承垂直反力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Choosing the wrong volume or direction misstates vertical trunnion reaction. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b250-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「雙鉸軸同軸量測」與「軸承摩擦與啟閉」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Trunnion coaxiality surveying\" and \"Bearing friction and operation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b250-v15-09","title":"雙鉸軸同軸量測：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Trunnion coaxiality surveying: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「雙鉸軸同軸量測」如何影響大型弧形閘門安裝的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Trunnion coaxiality surveying” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Large radial-gate installation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"左右鉸軸需要符合設計同軸與高程條件，偏差會使支臂扭曲並增加軸承摩擦。兩端高差除跨度只是小角度幾何示意，不代表完整三維同軸誤差；還需量測軸線方向、支座位置與溫度變化後的相對移動。 驗證時應以獨立控制網量測兩鉸軸中心與方向並核對溫度，並辨識以下失效情境：只核對中心高程會漏掉軸線方向偏斜。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「雙鉸軸同軸量測」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Both trunnions must satisfy alignment and elevation requirements. Misalignment twists arms and raises bearing friction. End-height difference divided by span illustrates one small-angle component, not full three-dimensional coaxiality; also survey axis orientation, support positions and temperature-dependent relative movement. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Survey both trunnion centers and directions from an independent network and record temperature. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Checking center elevations alone misses angular axis misalignment. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Trunnion coaxiality surveying” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：endElevationDifference=3 mm; span=10000 mm; smallAngle=3/10000=0.000300 rad。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: endElevationDifference=3 mm; span=10000 mm; smallAngle=3/10000=0.000300 rad.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩鉸中心同高就保證三維軸線完全同軸」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal trunnion-center elevations guarantee complete three-dimensional coaxiality\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「雙鉸軸同軸量測」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Trunnion coaxiality surveying”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-09-k1","title":"雙鉸軸同軸量測","titleEn":"Trunnion coaxiality surveying","text":"左右鉸軸需要符合設計同軸與高程條件，偏差會使支臂扭曲並增加軸承摩擦。兩端高差除跨度只是小角度幾何示意，不代表完整三維同軸誤差；還需量測軸線方向、支座位置與溫度變化後的相對移動。","textEn":"Both trunnions must satisfy alignment and elevation requirements. Misalignment twists arms and raises bearing friction.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩鉸中心同高就保證三維軸線完全同軸 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal trunnion-center elevations guarantee complete three-dimensional coaxiality Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「雙鉸軸同軸量測」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Trunnion coaxiality surveying\" is correct?","options":["左右鉸軸需要符合設計同軸與高程條件，偏差會使支臂扭曲並增加軸承摩擦。","兩鉸中心同高就保證三維軸線完全同軸","軸承反力不變就表示摩擦力矩永遠不變"],"optionsEn":["Both trunnions must satisfy alignment and elevation requirements.","Equal trunnion-center elevations guarantee complete three-dimensional coaxiality","Constant bearing reaction guarantees constant friction torque"],"answer":0,"explanation":"左右鉸軸需要符合設計同軸與高程條件，偏差會使支臂扭曲並增加軸承摩擦。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Both trunnions must satisfy alignment and elevation requirements. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b250-v15-10","title":"雙鉸軸同軸量測：定量估算","titleEn":"Trunnion coaxiality surveying: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「雙鉸軸同軸量測」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Trunnion coaxiality surveying” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：endElevationDifference=3 mm; span=10000 mm; smallAngle=3/10000=0.000300 rad。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: endElevationDifference=3 mm; span=10000 mm; smallAngle=3/10000=0.000300 rad. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以獨立控制網量測兩鉸軸中心與方向並核對溫度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Survey both trunnion centers and directions from an independent network and record temperature.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：endElevationDifference=3 mm; span=10000 mm; smallAngle=3/10000=0.000300 rad。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: endElevationDifference=3 mm; span=10000 mm; smallAngle=3/10000=0.000300 rad. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「雙鉸軸同軸量測」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Trunnion coaxiality surveying\", which statement holds?","options":["面板總面積相同就保證局部彎曲完全相同","原創教學假設：endElevationDifference=3 mm; span=10000 mm; smallAngle=3/10000=0.000300 rad。","總拉力除錨栓數就是每支錨栓的實際最大力"],"optionsEn":["Equal total skin area guarantees identical local bending","Original teaching assumptions: endElevationDifference=3 mm; span=10000 mm; smallAngle=3/10000=0.000300 rad.","Total tension divided by anchor count equals every anchor maximum"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：endElevationDifference=3 mm; span=10000 mm; smallAngle=3/10000=0.000300 rad。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: endElevationDifference=3 mm; span=10000 mm; smallAngle=3/10000=0.000300 rad. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b250-v15-11","title":"雙鉸軸同軸量測：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Trunnion coaxiality surveying: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「雙鉸軸同軸量測」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Trunnion coaxiality surveying” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以獨立控制網量測兩鉸軸中心與方向並核對溫度。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只核對中心高程會漏掉軸線方向偏斜」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Survey both trunnion centers and directions from an independent network and record temperature. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Checking center elevations alone misses angular axis misalignment. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以獨立控制網量測兩鉸軸中心與方向並核對溫度作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只核對中心高程會漏掉軸線方向偏斜，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Survey both trunnion centers and directions from an independent network and record temperature. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Checking center elevations alone misses angular axis misalignment. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：只核對中心高程會漏掉軸線方向偏斜。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Checking center elevations alone misses angular axis misalignment. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以獨立控制網量測兩鉸軸中心與方向並核對溫度。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只核對中心高程會漏掉軸線方向偏斜」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Survey both trunnion centers and directions from an independent network and record temperature. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Checking center elevations alone misses angular axis misalignment. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以獨立控制網量測兩鉸軸中心與方向並核對溫度作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只核對中心高程會漏掉軸線方向偏斜，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Survey both trunnion centers and directions from an independent network and record temperature. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Checking center elevations alone misses angular axis misalignment. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「雙鉸軸同軸量測」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Trunnion coaxiality surveying\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","兩側位置讀值相同就保證兩側荷載相同","以獨立控制網量測兩鉸軸中心與方向並核對溫度。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Equal side-position readings guarantee equal loads on both sides","Survey both trunnion centers and directions from an independent network and record temperature."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以獨立控制網量測兩鉸軸中心與方向並核對溫度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Survey both trunnion centers and directions from an independent network and record temperature. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b250-v15-12","title":"雙鉸軸同軸量測：失效診斷","titleEn":"Trunnion coaxiality surveying: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「雙鉸軸同軸量測」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Trunnion coaxiality surveying” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只核對中心高程會漏掉軸線方向偏斜。診斷時應採取以下查核：以獨立控制網量測兩鉸軸中心與方向並核對溫度，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Checking center elevations alone misses angular axis misalignment. Diagnose it by the following check: Survey both trunnion centers and directions from an independent network and record temperature. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩鉸中心同高就保證三維軸線完全同軸」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal trunnion-center elevations guarantee complete three-dimensional coaxiality\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只核對中心高程會漏掉軸線方向偏斜。診斷時應採取以下查核：以獨立控制網量測兩鉸軸中心與方向並核對溫度，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Checking center elevations alone misses angular axis misalignment. Diagnose it by the following check: Survey both trunnion centers and directions from an independent network and record temperature. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「雙鉸軸同軸量測」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Trunnion coaxiality surveying\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只核對中心高程會漏掉軸線方向偏斜。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","軸承反力不變就表示摩擦力矩永遠不變"],"optionsEn":["Checking center elevations alone misses angular axis misalignment.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Constant bearing reaction guarantees constant friction torque"],"answer":0,"explanation":"只核對中心高程會漏掉軸線方向偏斜。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Checking center elevations alone misses angular axis misalignment. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b250-v15-13","title":"軸承摩擦與啟閉：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Bearing friction and operation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「軸承摩擦與啟閉」如何影響大型弧形閘門安裝的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Bearing friction and operation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Large radial-gate installation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"鉸軸摩擦把支承反力轉成阻力矩，潤滑不足、鏽蝕與偏心會改變摩擦係數。簡化庫侖摩擦式只估給定接觸狀態的量級，不能保證啟動與運轉摩擦相同；驗證應比較鉸反力、啟動力及運轉後溫升趨勢。 驗證時應比較啟動與穩定運轉的馬達電流及軸承溫升，並辨識以下失效情境：摩擦上升可能把額外彎矩傳入原本主要受壓支臂。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「軸承摩擦與啟閉」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Trunnion friction converts bearing reaction into resisting torque. Lubrication, corrosion and misalignment change the coefficient. A Coulomb estimate describes a specified contact state and does not make breakaway and running friction identical; compare reaction, starting demand and subsequent temperature trends. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare motor current at breakaway and steady travel with bearing temperature rise. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Rising friction can introduce additional bending into primarily compressed arms. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Bearing friction and operation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：bearingReaction=1800 kN; frictionCoefficient=0.08; effectiveRadius=0.20 m; frictionTorque=1800*0.08*0.20=28.8 kN*m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: bearingReaction=1800 kN; frictionCoefficient=0.08; effectiveRadius=0.20 m; frictionTorque=1800*0.08*0.20=28.8 kN*m.","failure":"常見誤解：「軸承反力不變就表示摩擦力矩永遠不變」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Constant bearing reaction guarantees constant friction torque\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「軸承摩擦與啟閉」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Bearing friction and operation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-13-k1","title":"軸承摩擦與啟閉","titleEn":"Bearing friction and operation","text":"鉸軸摩擦把支承反力轉成阻力矩，潤滑不足、鏽蝕與偏心會改變摩擦係數。簡化庫侖摩擦式只估給定接觸狀態的量級，不能保證啟動與運轉摩擦相同；驗證應比較鉸反力、啟動力及運轉後溫升趨勢。","textEn":"Trunnion friction converts bearing reaction into resisting torque. Lubrication, corrosion and misalignment change the coefficient.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：軸承反力不變就表示摩擦力矩永遠不變 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Constant bearing reaction guarantees constant friction torque Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「軸承摩擦與啟閉」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bearing friction and operation\" is correct?","options":["軸承反力不變就表示摩擦力矩永遠不變","鉸軸摩擦把支承反力轉成阻力矩，潤滑不足、鏽蝕與偏心會改變摩擦係數。","兩根吊索不論角度都各承受總重的一半"],"optionsEn":["Constant bearing reaction guarantees constant friction torque","Trunnion friction converts bearing reaction into resisting torque.","Two slings each carry half the weight regardless of angle"],"answer":1,"explanation":"鉸軸摩擦把支承反力轉成阻力矩，潤滑不足、鏽蝕與偏心會改變摩擦係數。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Trunnion friction converts bearing reaction into resisting torque. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b250-v15-14","title":"軸承摩擦與啟閉：定量估算","titleEn":"Bearing friction and operation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「軸承摩擦與啟閉」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Bearing friction and operation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：bearingReaction=1800 kN; frictionCoefficient=0.08; effectiveRadius=0.20 m; frictionTorque=1800*0.08*0.20=28.8 kN*m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: bearingReaction=1800 kN; frictionCoefficient=0.08; effectiveRadius=0.20 m; frictionTorque=1800*0.08*0.20=28.8 kN*m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較啟動與穩定運轉的馬達電流及軸承溫升。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare motor current at breakaway and steady travel with bearing temperature rise.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：bearingReaction=1800 kN; frictionCoefficient=0.08; effectiveRadius=0.20 m; frictionTorque=1800*0.08*0.20=28.8 kN*m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: bearingReaction=1800 kN; frictionCoefficient=0.08; effectiveRadius=0.20 m; frictionTorque=1800*0.08*0.20=28.8 kN*m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「軸承摩擦與啟閉」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bearing friction and operation\", which statement holds?","options":["理想歐拉屈曲力就是現場支臂可直接承受荷載","止水壓縮越多就必定越好且沒有代價","原創教學假設：bearingReaction=1800 kN; frictionCoefficient=0.08; effectiveRadius=0.20 m; frictionTorque=1800*0.08*0.20=28.8 kN*m。"],"optionsEn":["Ideal Euler load is the directly usable field capacity of the arm","More seal compression is always better and has no adverse effect","Original teaching assumptions: bearingReaction=1800 kN; frictionCoefficient=0.08; effectiveRadius=0.20 m; frictionTorque=1800*0.08*0.20=28.8 kN*m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：bearingReaction=1800 kN; frictionCoefficient=0.08; effectiveRadius=0.20 m; frictionTorque=1800*0.08*0.20=28.8 kN*m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: bearingReaction=1800 kN; frictionCoefficient=0.08; effectiveRadius=0.20 m; frictionTorque=1800*0.08*0.20=28.8 kN*m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b250-v15-15","title":"軸承摩擦與啟閉：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bearing friction and operation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「軸承摩擦與啟閉」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Bearing friction and operation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較啟動與穩定運轉的馬達電流及軸承溫升。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「摩擦上升可能把額外彎矩傳入原本主要受壓支臂」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare motor current at breakaway and steady travel with bearing temperature rise. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Rising friction can introduce additional bending into primarily compressed arms. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以比較啟動與穩定運轉的馬達電流及軸承溫升作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對摩擦上升可能把額外彎矩傳入原本主要受壓支臂，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare motor current at breakaway and steady travel with bearing temperature rise. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Rising friction can introduce additional bending into primarily compressed arms. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：摩擦上升可能把額外彎矩傳入原本主要受壓支臂。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Rising friction can introduce additional bending into primarily compressed arms. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較啟動與穩定運轉的馬達電流及軸承溫升。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「摩擦上升可能把額外彎矩傳入原本主要受壓支臂」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare motor current at breakaway and steady travel with bearing temperature rise. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Rising friction can introduce additional bending into primarily compressed arms. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以比較啟動與穩定運轉的馬達電流及軸承溫升作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對摩擦上升可能把額外彎矩傳入原本主要受壓支臂，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare motor current at breakaway and steady travel with bearing temperature rise. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Rising friction can introduce additional bending into primarily compressed arms. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「軸承摩擦與啟閉」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bearing friction and operation\"?","options":["比較啟動與穩定運轉的馬達電流及軸承溫升。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","理想弧門水壓通過鉸軸就代表全部荷載皆無力矩"],"optionsEn":["Compare motor current at breakaway and steady travel with bearing temperature rise.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Pressure passing through the trunnion means every gate load has zero moment"],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較啟動與穩定運轉的馬達電流及軸承溫升。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare motor current at breakaway and steady travel with bearing temperature rise. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b250-v15-16","title":"軸承摩擦與啟閉：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bearing friction and operation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「軸承摩擦與啟閉」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Bearing friction and operation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"摩擦上升可能把額外彎矩傳入原本主要受壓支臂。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較啟動與穩定運轉的馬達電流及軸承溫升，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Rising friction can introduce additional bending into primarily compressed arms. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare motor current at breakaway and steady travel with bearing temperature rise. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「軸承反力不變就表示摩擦力矩永遠不變」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Constant bearing reaction guarantees constant friction torque\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"摩擦上升可能把額外彎矩傳入原本主要受壓支臂。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較啟動與穩定運轉的馬達電流及軸承溫升，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Rising friction can introduce additional bending into primarily compressed arms. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare motor current at breakaway and steady travel with bearing temperature rise. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「軸承摩擦與啟閉」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bearing friction and operation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","摩擦上升可能把額外彎矩傳入原本主要受壓支臂。","兩根吊索不論角度都各承受總重的一半"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Rising friction can introduce additional bending into primarily compressed arms.","Two slings each carry half the weight regardless of angle"],"answer":1,"explanation":"摩擦上升可能把額外彎矩傳入原本主要受壓支臂。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Rising friction can introduce additional bending into primarily compressed arms. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b250-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「吊索角度與張力」與「面板支承間彎曲」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Sling angle and tension\" and \"Skinplate bending between supports\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b250-v15-17","title":"吊索角度與張力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Sling angle and tension: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「吊索角度與張力」如何影響大型弧形閘門安裝的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sling angle and tension” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Large radial-gate installation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"門葉組裝吊運需依實際重心配置吊點，斜索張力會隨索角變小而增加。對稱兩索公式只適用靜態對稱分載，重心偏移、動態放大與吊具剛度需另列；教學幾何不能取代核准吊裝計畫與現場試吊觀測。 驗證時應以吊點荷重讀值核對分載並確認重心與吊索角度，並辨識以下失效情境：重心偏移可讓單側吊索超出對稱分載估計。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「吊索角度與張力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Assembly lifting requires pick points compatible with the actual center of mass. Sling tension increases as inclination becomes shallow. The symmetric two-sling equation assumes static equal sharing; eccentricity, dynamics and rigging stiffness require separate allowances and an approved lifting plan with observed load behavior. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Check sharing with pick-point load readings and confirm center of mass and sling angles. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: An offset center of mass can overload one sling relative to symmetric sharing. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Sling angle and tension” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：totalWeight=400 kN; two symmetric slings60 degrees above horizontal; eachTension=400/(2*sin(60 degrees))=230.940 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: totalWeight=400 kN; two symmetric slings60 degrees above horizontal; eachTension=400/(2*sin(60 degrees))=230.940 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩根吊索不論角度都各承受總重的一半」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two slings each carry half the weight regardless of angle\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「吊索角度與張力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Sling angle and tension”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-17-k1","title":"吊索角度與張力","titleEn":"Sling angle and tension","text":"門葉組裝吊運需依實際重心配置吊點，斜索張力會隨索角變小而增加。對稱兩索公式只適用靜態對稱分載，重心偏移、動態放大與吊具剛度需另列；教學幾何不能取代核准吊裝計畫與現場試吊觀測。","textEn":"Assembly lifting requires pick points compatible with the actual center of mass. Sling tension increases as inclination becomes shallow.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩根吊索不論角度都各承受總重的一半 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two slings each carry half the weight regardless of angle Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「吊索角度與張力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Sling angle and tension\" is correct?","options":["兩根吊索不論角度都各承受總重的一半","面板總面積相同就保證局部彎曲完全相同","門葉組裝吊運需依實際重心配置吊點，斜索張力會隨索角變小而增加。"],"optionsEn":["Two slings each carry half the weight regardless of angle","Equal total skin area guarantees identical local bending","Assembly lifting requires pick points compatible with the actual center of mass."],"answer":2,"explanation":"門葉組裝吊運需依實際重心配置吊點，斜索張力會隨索角變小而增加。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Assembly lifting requires pick points compatible with the actual center of mass. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b250-v15-18","title":"吊索角度與張力：定量估算","titleEn":"Sling angle and tension: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「吊索角度與張力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sling angle and tension” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：totalWeight=400 kN; two symmetric slings60 degrees above horizontal; eachTension=400/(2*sin(60 degrees))=230.940 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: totalWeight=400 kN; two symmetric slings60 degrees above horizontal; eachTension=400/(2*sin(60 degrees))=230.940 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以吊點荷重讀值核對分載並確認重心與吊索角度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check sharing with pick-point load readings and confirm center of mass and sling angles.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：totalWeight=400 kN; two symmetric slings60 degrees above horizontal; eachTension=400/(2*sin(60 degrees))=230.940 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: totalWeight=400 kN; two symmetric slings60 degrees above horizontal; eachTension=400/(2*sin(60 degrees))=230.940 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「吊索角度與張力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Sling angle and tension\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：totalWeight=400 kN; two symmetric slings60 degrees above horizontal; eachTension=400/(2*sin(60 degrees))=230.940 kN。","總拉力除錨栓數就是每支錨栓的實際最大力","兩側位置讀值相同就保證兩側荷載相同"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: totalWeight=400 kN; two symmetric slings60 degrees above horizontal; eachTension=400/(2*sin(60 degrees))=230.940 kN.","Total tension divided by anchor count equals every anchor maximum","Equal side-position readings guarantee equal loads on both sides"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：totalWeight=400 kN; two symmetric slings60 degrees above horizontal; eachTension=400/(2*sin(60 degrees))=230.940 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: totalWeight=400 kN; two symmetric slings60 degrees above horizontal; eachTension=400/(2*sin(60 degrees))=230.940 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b250-v15-19","title":"吊索角度與張力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Sling angle and tension: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「吊索角度與張力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Sling angle and tension” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以吊點荷重讀值核對分載並確認重心與吊索角度。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「重心偏移可讓單側吊索超出對稱分載估計」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check sharing with pick-point load readings and confirm center of mass and sling angles. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: An offset center of mass can overload one sling relative to symmetric sharing. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以吊點荷重讀值核對分載並確認重心與吊索角度作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對重心偏移可讓單側吊索超出對稱分載估計，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check sharing with pick-point load readings and confirm center of mass and sling angles. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: An offset center of mass can overload one sling relative to symmetric sharing. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：重心偏移可讓單側吊索超出對稱分載估計。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An offset center of mass can overload one sling relative to symmetric sharing. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以吊點荷重讀值核對分載並確認重心與吊索角度。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「重心偏移可讓單側吊索超出對稱分載估計」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Check sharing with pick-point load readings and confirm center of mass and sling angles. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: An offset center of mass can overload one sling relative to symmetric sharing. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以吊點荷重讀值核對分載並確認重心與吊索角度作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對重心偏移可讓單側吊索超出對稱分載估計，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check sharing with pick-point load readings and confirm center of mass and sling angles. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: An offset center of mass can overload one sling relative to symmetric sharing. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「吊索角度與張力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Sling angle and tension\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","以吊點荷重讀值核對分載並確認重心與吊索角度。","曲面面積乘平均壓力必然就是垂直水壓力"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Check sharing with pick-point load readings and confirm center of mass and sling angles.","Curved area times mean pressure always equals vertical hydrostatic force"],"answer":1,"explanation":"以吊點荷重讀值核對分載並確認重心與吊索角度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check sharing with pick-point load readings and confirm center of mass and sling angles. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b250-v15-20","title":"吊索角度與張力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Sling angle and tension: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「吊索角度與張力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Sling angle and tension” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"重心偏移可讓單側吊索超出對稱分載估計。診斷時應採取以下查核：以吊點荷重讀值核對分載並確認重心與吊索角度，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An offset center of mass can overload one sling relative to symmetric sharing. Diagnose it by the following check: Check sharing with pick-point load readings and confirm center of mass and sling angles. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩根吊索不論角度都各承受總重的一半」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two slings each carry half the weight regardless of angle\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"重心偏移可讓單側吊索超出對稱分載估計。診斷時應採取以下查核：以吊點荷重讀值核對分載並確認重心與吊索角度，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"An offset center of mass can overload one sling relative to symmetric sharing. Diagnose it by the following check: Check sharing with pick-point load readings and confirm center of mass and sling angles. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「吊索角度與張力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Sling angle and tension\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","面板總面積相同就保證局部彎曲完全相同","重心偏移可讓單側吊索超出對稱分載估計。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Equal total skin area guarantees identical local bending","An offset center of mass can overload one sling relative to symmetric sharing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"重心偏移可讓單側吊索超出對稱分載估計。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An offset center of mass can overload one sling relative to symmetric sharing. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b250-v15-21","title":"面板支承間彎曲：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Skinplate bending between supports: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「面板支承間彎曲」如何影響大型弧形閘門安裝的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Skinplate bending between supports” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Large radial-gate installation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"門葉面板把分布水壓傳到肋材，再經主梁與支臂送至鉸軸，支承距離會強烈影響局部彎曲。簡支條帶模型只示範一維傳力，實際板的雙向作用、焊接拘束與曲率需另分析；驗證須核對肋距及面板厚度。 驗證時應量測肋間距與板厚並比較受水壓後局部撓度，並辨識以下失效情境：肋材漏焊或接續不良可能延長實際無支承跨度。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「面板支承間彎曲」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The skin transfers distributed pressure to stiffeners, girders and arms. Support spacing strongly affects local bending. A simply supported strip illustrates one-dimensional action only; plate action, welded restraint and curvature need separate treatment. Verify actual stiffener spacing and thickness before comparing measured deformation. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Measure stiffener spacing and thickness and compare local deflection under water pressure. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Missing or defective stiffener welds can increase the effective unsupported span. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Skinplate bending between supports” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Unit-width strip: pressure=50 kPa; lineLoad=50 kN/m; span=1.2 m; simpleBeamMoment=50*1.2**2/8=9 kN*m per1m strip。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Unit-width strip: pressure=50 kPa; lineLoad=50 kN/m; span=1.2 m; simpleBeamMoment=50*1.2**2/8=9 kN*m per1m strip.","failure":"常見誤解：「面板總面積相同就保證局部彎曲完全相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal total skin area guarantees identical local bending\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「面板支承間彎曲」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Skinplate bending between supports”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-21-k1","title":"面板支承間彎曲","titleEn":"Skinplate bending between supports","text":"門葉面板把分布水壓傳到肋材，再經主梁與支臂送至鉸軸，支承距離會強烈影響局部彎曲。簡支條帶模型只示範一維傳力，實際板的雙向作用、焊接拘束與曲率需另分析；驗證須核對肋距及面板厚度。","textEn":"The skin transfers distributed pressure to stiffeners, girders and arms. Support spacing strongly affects local bending.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：面板總面積相同就保證局部彎曲完全相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal total skin area guarantees identical local bending Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「面板支承間彎曲」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Skinplate bending between supports\" is correct?","options":["門葉面板把分布水壓傳到肋材，再經主梁與支臂送至鉸軸，支承距離會強烈影響局部彎曲。","面板總面積相同就保證局部彎曲完全相同","理想歐拉屈曲力就是現場支臂可直接承受荷載"],"optionsEn":["The skin transfers distributed pressure to stiffeners, girders and arms.","Equal total skin area guarantees identical local bending","Ideal Euler load is the directly usable field capacity of the arm"],"answer":0,"explanation":"門葉面板把分布水壓傳到肋材，再經主梁與支臂送至鉸軸，支承距離會強烈影響局部彎曲。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The skin transfers distributed pressure to stiffeners, girders and arms. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b250-v15-22","title":"面板支承間彎曲：定量估算","titleEn":"Skinplate bending between supports: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「面板支承間彎曲」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Skinplate bending between supports” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Unit-width strip: pressure=50 kPa; lineLoad=50 kN/m; span=1.2 m; simpleBeamMoment=50*1.2**2/8=9 kN*m per1m strip。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Unit-width strip: pressure=50 kPa; lineLoad=50 kN/m; span=1.2 m; simpleBeamMoment=50*1.2**2/8=9 kN*m per1m strip. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量測肋間距與板厚並比較受水壓後局部撓度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure stiffener spacing and thickness and compare local deflection under water pressure.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Unit-width strip: pressure=50 kPa; lineLoad=50 kN/m; span=1.2 m; simpleBeamMoment=50*1.2**2/8=9 kN*m per1m strip。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Unit-width strip: pressure=50 kPa; lineLoad=50 kN/m; span=1.2 m; simpleBeamMoment=50*1.2**2/8=9 kN*m per1m strip. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「面板支承間彎曲」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Skinplate bending between supports\", which statement holds?","options":["止水壓縮越多就必定越好且沒有代價","原創教學假設：Unit-width strip: pressure=50 kPa; lineLoad=50 kN/m; span=1.2 m; simpleBeamMoment=50*1.2**2/8=9 kN*m per1m strip。","理想弧門水壓通過鉸軸就代表全部荷載皆無力矩"],"optionsEn":["More seal compression is always better and has no adverse effect","Original teaching assumptions: Unit-width strip: pressure=50 kPa; lineLoad=50 kN/m; span=1.2 m; simpleBeamMoment=50*1.2**2/8=9 kN*m per1m strip.","Pressure passing through the trunnion means every gate load has zero moment"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Unit-width strip: pressure=50 kPa; lineLoad=50 kN/m; span=1.2 m; simpleBeamMoment=50*1.2**2/8=9 kN*m per1m strip。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Unit-width strip: pressure=50 kPa; lineLoad=50 kN/m; span=1.2 m; simpleBeamMoment=50*1.2**2/8=9 kN*m per1m strip. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b250-v15-23","title":"面板支承間彎曲：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Skinplate bending between supports: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「面板支承間彎曲」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Skinplate bending between supports” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量測肋間距與板厚並比較受水壓後局部撓度。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「肋材漏焊或接續不良可能延長實際無支承跨度」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure stiffener spacing and thickness and compare local deflection under water pressure. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Missing or defective stiffener welds can increase the effective unsupported span. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以量測肋間距與板厚並比較受水壓後局部撓度作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對肋材漏焊或接續不良可能延長實際無支承跨度，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure stiffener spacing and thickness and compare local deflection under water pressure. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Missing or defective stiffener welds can increase the effective unsupported span. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：肋材漏焊或接續不良可能延長實際無支承跨度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Missing or defective stiffener welds can increase the effective unsupported span. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量測肋間距與板厚並比較受水壓後局部撓度。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「肋材漏焊或接續不良可能延長實際無支承跨度」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Measure stiffener spacing and thickness and compare local deflection under water pressure. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Missing or defective stiffener welds can increase the effective unsupported span. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以量測肋間距與板厚並比較受水壓後局部撓度作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對肋材漏焊或接續不良可能延長實際無支承跨度，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure stiffener spacing and thickness and compare local deflection under water pressure. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Missing or defective stiffener welds can increase the effective unsupported span. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「面板支承間彎曲」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Skinplate bending between supports\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","兩鉸中心同高就保證三維軸線完全同軸","量測肋間距與板厚並比較受水壓後局部撓度。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Equal trunnion-center elevations guarantee complete three-dimensional coaxiality","Measure stiffener spacing and thickness and compare local deflection under water pressure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量測肋間距與板厚並比較受水壓後局部撓度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure stiffener spacing and thickness and compare local deflection under water pressure. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b250-v15-24","title":"面板支承間彎曲：失效診斷","titleEn":"Skinplate bending between supports: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「面板支承間彎曲」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Skinplate bending between supports” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"肋材漏焊或接續不良可能延長實際無支承跨度。診斷時應採取以下查核：量測肋間距與板厚並比較受水壓後局部撓度，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Missing or defective stiffener welds can increase the effective unsupported span. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure stiffener spacing and thickness and compare local deflection under water pressure. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「面板總面積相同就保證局部彎曲完全相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal total skin area guarantees identical local bending\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"肋材漏焊或接續不良可能延長實際無支承跨度。診斷時應採取以下查核：量測肋間距與板厚並比較受水壓後局部撓度，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Missing or defective stiffener welds can increase the effective unsupported span. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure stiffener spacing and thickness and compare local deflection under water pressure. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「面板支承間彎曲」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Skinplate bending between supports\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["肋材漏焊或接續不良可能延長實際無支承跨度。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","理想歐拉屈曲力就是現場支臂可直接承受荷載"],"optionsEn":["Missing or defective stiffener welds can increase the effective unsupported span.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Ideal Euler load is the directly usable field capacity of the arm"],"answer":0,"explanation":"肋材漏焊或接續不良可能延長實際無支承跨度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Missing or defective stiffener welds can increase the effective unsupported span. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b250-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「支臂長細與屈曲」與「支座錨定與分載」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Arm slenderness and buckling\" and \"Support anchorage and load sharing\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b250-v15-25","title":"支臂長細與屈曲：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Arm slenderness and buckling: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「支臂長細與屈曲」如何影響大型弧形閘門安裝的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Arm slenderness and buckling” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Large radial-gate installation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"支臂承受壓力時需檢查整體穩定與局部板件屈曲，端部拘束會影響有效長度。歐拉公式僅適用理想彈性細長柱，不涵蓋初始彎曲、殘餘應力與組合彎矩；安裝偏差應進入模型而非只驗收截面積。 驗證時應核對支臂初始直線度接點拘束與局部板件尺寸，並辨識以下失效情境：鉸軸摩擦或偏心彎矩會降低理想軸壓模型的適用性。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「支臂長細與屈曲」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Compressed arms require global and local stability checks. End restraint affects effective length. Euler theory applies to an ideal elastic slender member and omits imperfections, residual stress and combined bending; installed deviations belong in the model rather than being ignored after checking area alone. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Check arm straightness, connection restraint and local plate dimensions. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Trunnion friction or eccentric bending invalidates a purely axial idealization. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Arm slenderness and buckling” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Ideal pinned elastic column: E=200e9 Pa; I=0.00008 m4; L=6 m; Pcr=pi**2*200e9*0.00008/6**2/1000=4386.49 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Ideal pinned elastic column: E=200e9 Pa; I=0.00008 m4; L=6 m; Pcr=pi**2*200e9*0.00008/6**2/1000=4386.49 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「理想歐拉屈曲力就是現場支臂可直接承受荷載」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Ideal Euler load is the directly usable field capacity of the arm\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「支臂長細與屈曲」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Arm slenderness and buckling”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-25-k1","title":"支臂長細與屈曲","titleEn":"Arm slenderness and buckling","text":"支臂承受壓力時需檢查整體穩定與局部板件屈曲，端部拘束會影響有效長度。歐拉公式僅適用理想彈性細長柱，不涵蓋初始彎曲、殘餘應力與組合彎矩；安裝偏差應進入模型而非只驗收截面積。","textEn":"Compressed arms require global and local stability checks. End restraint affects effective length.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：理想歐拉屈曲力就是現場支臂可直接承受荷載 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Ideal Euler load is the directly usable field capacity of the arm Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「支臂長細與屈曲」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Arm slenderness and buckling\" is correct?","options":["理想歐拉屈曲力就是現場支臂可直接承受荷載","支臂承受壓力時需檢查整體穩定與局部板件屈曲，端部拘束會影響有效長度。","總拉力除錨栓數就是每支錨栓的實際最大力"],"optionsEn":["Ideal Euler load is the directly usable field capacity of the arm","Compressed arms require global and local stability checks.","Total tension divided by anchor count equals every anchor maximum"],"answer":1,"explanation":"支臂承受壓力時需檢查整體穩定與局部板件屈曲，端部拘束會影響有效長度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Compressed arms require global and local stability checks. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b250-v15-26","title":"支臂長細與屈曲：定量估算","titleEn":"Arm slenderness and buckling: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「支臂長細與屈曲」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Arm slenderness and buckling” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Ideal pinned elastic column: E=200e9 Pa; I=0.00008 m4; L=6 m; Pcr=pi**2*200e9*0.00008/6**2/1000=4386.49 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Ideal pinned elastic column: E=200e9 Pa; I=0.00008 m4; L=6 m; Pcr=pi**2*200e9*0.00008/6**2/1000=4386.49 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對支臂初始直線度接點拘束與局部板件尺寸。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check arm straightness, connection restraint and local plate dimensions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Ideal pinned elastic column: E=200e9 Pa; I=0.00008 m4; L=6 m; Pcr=pi**2*200e9*0.00008/6**2/1000=4386.49 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Ideal pinned elastic column: E=200e9 Pa; I=0.00008 m4; L=6 m; Pcr=pi**2*200e9*0.00008/6**2/1000=4386.49 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「支臂長細與屈曲」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Arm slenderness and buckling\", which statement holds?","options":["兩側位置讀值相同就保證兩側荷載相同","曲面面積乘平均壓力必然就是垂直水壓力","原創教學假設：Ideal pinned elastic column: E=200e9 Pa; I=0.00008 m4; L=6 m; Pcr=pi**2*200e9*0.00008/6**2/1000=4386.49 kN。"],"optionsEn":["Equal side-position readings guarantee equal loads on both sides","Curved area times mean pressure always equals vertical hydrostatic force","Original teaching assumptions: Ideal pinned elastic column: E=200e9 Pa; I=0.00008 m4; L=6 m; Pcr=pi**2*200e9*0.00008/6**2/1000=4386.49 kN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Ideal pinned elastic column: E=200e9 Pa; I=0.00008 m4; L=6 m; Pcr=pi**2*200e9*0.00008/6**2/1000=4386.49 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Ideal pinned elastic column: E=200e9 Pa; I=0.00008 m4; L=6 m; Pcr=pi**2*200e9*0.00008/6**2/1000=4386.49 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b250-v15-27","title":"支臂長細與屈曲：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Arm slenderness and buckling: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「支臂長細與屈曲」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Arm slenderness and buckling” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對支臂初始直線度接點拘束與局部板件尺寸。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「鉸軸摩擦或偏心彎矩會降低理想軸壓模型的適用性」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check arm straightness, connection restraint and local plate dimensions. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Trunnion friction or eccentric bending invalidates a purely axial idealization. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以核對支臂初始直線度接點拘束與局部板件尺寸作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對鉸軸摩擦或偏心彎矩會降低理想軸壓模型的適用性，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check arm straightness, connection restraint and local plate dimensions. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Trunnion friction or eccentric bending invalidates a purely axial idealization. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：鉸軸摩擦或偏心彎矩會降低理想軸壓模型的適用性。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Trunnion friction or eccentric bending invalidates a purely axial idealization. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對支臂初始直線度接點拘束與局部板件尺寸。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「鉸軸摩擦或偏心彎矩會降低理想軸壓模型的適用性」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Check arm straightness, connection restraint and local plate dimensions. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Trunnion friction or eccentric bending invalidates a purely axial idealization. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以核對支臂初始直線度接點拘束與局部板件尺寸作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對鉸軸摩擦或偏心彎矩會降低理想軸壓模型的適用性，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check arm straightness, connection restraint and local plate dimensions. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Trunnion friction or eccentric bending invalidates a purely axial idealization. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「支臂長細與屈曲」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Arm slenderness and buckling\"?","options":["核對支臂初始直線度接點拘束與局部板件尺寸。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","軸承反力不變就表示摩擦力矩永遠不變"],"optionsEn":["Check arm straightness, connection restraint and local plate dimensions.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Constant bearing reaction guarantees constant friction torque"],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對支臂初始直線度接點拘束與局部板件尺寸。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check arm straightness, connection restraint and local plate dimensions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b250-v15-28","title":"支臂長細與屈曲：失效診斷","titleEn":"Arm slenderness and buckling: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「支臂長細與屈曲」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Arm slenderness and buckling” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"鉸軸摩擦或偏心彎矩會降低理想軸壓模型的適用性。診斷時應採取以下查核：核對支臂初始直線度接點拘束與局部板件尺寸，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Trunnion friction or eccentric bending invalidates a purely axial idealization. Diagnose it by the following check: Check arm straightness, connection restraint and local plate dimensions. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「理想歐拉屈曲力就是現場支臂可直接承受荷載」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Ideal Euler load is the directly usable field capacity of the arm\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"鉸軸摩擦或偏心彎矩會降低理想軸壓模型的適用性。診斷時應採取以下查核：核對支臂初始直線度接點拘束與局部板件尺寸，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Trunnion friction or eccentric bending invalidates a purely axial idealization. Diagnose it by the following check: Check arm straightness, connection restraint and local plate dimensions. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「支臂長細與屈曲」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Arm slenderness and buckling\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","鉸軸摩擦或偏心彎矩會降低理想軸壓模型的適用性。","總拉力除錨栓數就是每支錨栓的實際最大力"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Trunnion friction or eccentric bending invalidates a purely axial idealization.","Total tension divided by anchor count equals every anchor maximum"],"answer":1,"explanation":"鉸軸摩擦或偏心彎矩會降低理想軸壓模型的適用性。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Trunnion friction or eccentric bending invalidates a purely axial idealization. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b250-v15-29","title":"支座錨定與分載：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Support anchorage and load sharing: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「支座錨定與分載」如何影響大型弧形閘門安裝的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Support anchorage and load sharing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Large radial-gate installation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"鉸支座透過底板、錨定與混凝土把反力傳入壩墩，各螺栓受力通常因偏心與底板彈性而不均。平均分載只能作帳務起點；灌漿空洞、預緊差異與裂縫會改變接觸及荷載路徑，須配合局部模型與檢測。 驗證時應核對預緊紀錄灌漿完整性與支座變形再比較分載，並辨識以下失效情境：底板局部離縫會把拉力集中到少數錨栓。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「支座錨定與分載」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Trunnion supports transfer load through plates, anchorage and concrete. Eccentricity and plate flexibility generally make bolt forces unequal. Equal sharing is only a bookkeeping start; grout voids, preload variation and cracking alter contact and load paths and need local analysis and inspection. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Review preload, grout continuity and support deformation before comparing load sharing. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Local baseplate separation concentrates tension in a few anchors. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Support anchorage and load sharing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Ideal centered tension=800 kN; eight equal-stiffness anchors; averageTension=800/8=100 kN per anchor。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Ideal centered tension=800 kN; eight equal-stiffness anchors; averageTension=800/8=100 kN per anchor.","failure":"常見誤解：「總拉力除錨栓數就是每支錨栓的實際最大力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Total tension divided by anchor count equals every anchor maximum\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「支座錨定與分載」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Support anchorage and load sharing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-29-k1","title":"支座錨定與分載","titleEn":"Support anchorage and load sharing","text":"鉸支座透過底板、錨定與混凝土把反力傳入壩墩，各螺栓受力通常因偏心與底板彈性而不均。平均分載只能作帳務起點；灌漿空洞、預緊差異與裂縫會改變接觸及荷載路徑，須配合局部模型與檢測。","textEn":"Trunnion supports transfer load through plates, anchorage and concrete. Eccentricity and plate flexibility generally make bolt forces unequal.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：總拉力除錨栓數就是每支錨栓的實際最大力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Total tension divided by anchor count equals every anchor maximum Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「支座錨定與分載」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Support anchorage and load sharing\" is correct?","options":["總拉力除錨栓數就是每支錨栓的實際最大力","止水壓縮越多就必定越好且沒有代價","鉸支座透過底板、錨定與混凝土把反力傳入壩墩，各螺栓受力通常因偏心與底板彈性而不均。"],"optionsEn":["Total tension divided by anchor count equals every anchor maximum","More seal compression is always better and has no adverse effect","Trunnion supports transfer load through plates, anchorage and concrete."],"answer":2,"explanation":"鉸支座透過底板、錨定與混凝土把反力傳入壩墩，各螺栓受力通常因偏心與底板彈性而不均。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Trunnion supports transfer load through plates, anchorage and concrete. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b250-v15-30","title":"支座錨定與分載：定量估算","titleEn":"Support anchorage and load sharing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「支座錨定與分載」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Support anchorage and load sharing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Ideal centered tension=800 kN; eight equal-stiffness anchors; averageTension=800/8=100 kN per anchor。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Ideal centered tension=800 kN; eight equal-stiffness anchors; averageTension=800/8=100 kN per anchor. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對預緊紀錄灌漿完整性與支座變形再比較分載。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Review preload, grout continuity and support deformation before comparing load sharing.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Ideal centered tension=800 kN; eight equal-stiffness anchors; averageTension=800/8=100 kN per anchor。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Ideal centered tension=800 kN; eight equal-stiffness anchors; averageTension=800/8=100 kN per anchor. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「支座錨定與分載」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Support anchorage and load sharing\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：Ideal centered tension=800 kN; eight equal-stiffness anchors; averageTension=800/8=100 kN per anchor。","理想弧門水壓通過鉸軸就代表全部荷載皆無力矩","兩鉸中心同高就保證三維軸線完全同軸"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: Ideal centered tension=800 kN; eight equal-stiffness anchors; averageTension=800/8=100 kN per anchor.","Pressure passing through the trunnion means every gate load has zero moment","Equal trunnion-center elevations guarantee complete three-dimensional coaxiality"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Ideal centered tension=800 kN; eight equal-stiffness anchors; averageTension=800/8=100 kN per anchor。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Ideal centered tension=800 kN; eight equal-stiffness anchors; averageTension=800/8=100 kN per anchor. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b250-v15-31","title":"支座錨定與分載：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Support anchorage and load sharing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「支座錨定與分載」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Support anchorage and load sharing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對預緊紀錄灌漿完整性與支座變形再比較分載。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「底板局部離縫會把拉力集中到少數錨栓」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Review preload, grout continuity and support deformation before comparing load sharing. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Local baseplate separation concentrates tension in a few anchors. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以核對預緊紀錄灌漿完整性與支座變形再比較分載作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對底板局部離縫會把拉力集中到少數錨栓，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Review preload, grout continuity and support deformation before comparing load sharing. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Local baseplate separation concentrates tension in a few anchors. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：底板局部離縫會把拉力集中到少數錨栓。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Local baseplate separation concentrates tension in a few anchors. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對預緊紀錄灌漿完整性與支座變形再比較分載。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「底板局部離縫會把拉力集中到少數錨栓」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Review preload, grout continuity and support deformation before comparing load sharing. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Local baseplate separation concentrates tension in a few anchors. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以核對預緊紀錄灌漿完整性與支座變形再比較分載作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對底板局部離縫會把拉力集中到少數錨栓，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Review preload, grout continuity and support deformation before comparing load sharing. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Local baseplate separation concentrates tension in a few anchors. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「支座錨定與分載」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Support anchorage and load sharing\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","核對預緊紀錄灌漿完整性與支座變形再比較分載。","兩根吊索不論角度都各承受總重的一半"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Review preload, grout continuity and support deformation before comparing load sharing.","Two slings each carry half the weight regardless of angle"],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對預緊紀錄灌漿完整性與支座變形再比較分載。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Review preload, grout continuity and support deformation before comparing load sharing. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b250-v15-32","title":"支座錨定與分載：失效診斷","titleEn":"Support anchorage and load sharing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「支座錨定與分載」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Support anchorage and load sharing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"底板局部離縫會把拉力集中到少數錨栓。診斷時應採取以下查核：核對預緊紀錄灌漿完整性與支座變形再比較分載，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Local baseplate separation concentrates tension in a few anchors. Diagnose it by the following check: Review preload, grout continuity and support deformation before comparing load sharing. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「總拉力除錨栓數就是每支錨栓的實際最大力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Total tension divided by anchor count equals every anchor maximum\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"底板局部離縫會把拉力集中到少數錨栓。診斷時應採取以下查核：核對預緊紀錄灌漿完整性與支座變形再比較分載，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Local baseplate separation concentrates tension in a few anchors. Diagnose it by the following check: Review preload, grout continuity and support deformation before comparing load sharing. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「支座錨定與分載」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Support anchorage and load sharing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","止水壓縮越多就必定越好且沒有代價","底板局部離縫會把拉力集中到少數錨栓。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","More seal compression is always better and has no adverse effect","Local baseplate separation concentrates tension in a few anchors."],"answer":2,"explanation":"底板局部離縫會把拉力集中到少數錨栓。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Local baseplate separation concentrates tension in a few anchors. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b250-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「側封壓縮與摩擦」與「同步行程與試運轉」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Side-seal compression and friction\" and \"Synchronized travel and commissioning\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b250-v15-33","title":"側封壓縮與摩擦：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Side-seal compression and friction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「側封壓縮與摩擦」如何影響大型弧形閘門安裝的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Side-seal compression and friction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Large radial-gate installation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"側封須在門葉運動範圍維持接觸，過少壓縮會漏水，過多則增加摩擦與磨耗。壓縮百分比是幾何量，不是接觸壓力的通用換算式；橡膠硬度、溫度與支承形狀需按供應商資料及實際接觸試驗確認。 驗證時應沿全行程量測封面接觸與啟閉阻力並定位滲漏，並辨識以下失效情境：偏斜門葉可使一側過壓縮而另一側失去密封。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「側封壓縮與摩擦」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Side seals need contact throughout travel. Too little compression leaks, while too much raises friction and wear. Compression percentage is geometry rather than a universal contact-pressure law; elastomer hardness, temperature and support shape require supplier information and representative contact testing. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Measure seal contact and operating resistance throughout travel and locate leakage. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: A skewed gate can overcompress one seal while unloading the other. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Side-seal compression and friction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：FreeSealThickness=30 mm; installedThickness=24 mm; compression=(30-24)/30*100=20 percent。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: FreeSealThickness=30 mm; installedThickness=24 mm; compression=(30-24)/30*100=20 percent.","failure":"常見誤解：「止水壓縮越多就必定越好且沒有代價」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"More seal compression is always better and has no adverse effect\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「側封壓縮與摩擦」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Side-seal compression and friction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-33-k1","title":"側封壓縮與摩擦","titleEn":"Side-seal compression and friction","text":"側封須在門葉運動範圍維持接觸，過少壓縮會漏水，過多則增加摩擦與磨耗。壓縮百分比是幾何量，不是接觸壓力的通用換算式；橡膠硬度、溫度與支承形狀需按供應商資料及實際接觸試驗確認。","textEn":"Side seals need contact throughout travel. Too little compression leaks, while too much raises friction and wear.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：止水壓縮越多就必定越好且沒有代價 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: More seal compression is always better and has no adverse effect Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「側封壓縮與摩擦」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Side-seal compression and friction\" is correct?","options":["側封須在門葉運動範圍維持接觸，過少壓縮會漏水，過多則增加摩擦與磨耗。","止水壓縮越多就必定越好且沒有代價","兩側位置讀值相同就保證兩側荷載相同"],"optionsEn":["Side seals need contact throughout travel.","More seal compression is always better and has no adverse effect","Equal side-position readings guarantee equal loads on both sides"],"answer":0,"explanation":"側封須在門葉運動範圍維持接觸，過少壓縮會漏水，過多則增加摩擦與磨耗。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Side seals need contact throughout travel. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b250-v15-34","title":"側封壓縮與摩擦：定量估算","titleEn":"Side-seal compression and friction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「側封壓縮與摩擦」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Side-seal compression and friction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：FreeSealThickness=30 mm; installedThickness=24 mm; compression=(30-24)/30*100=20 percent。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: FreeSealThickness=30 mm; installedThickness=24 mm; compression=(30-24)/30*100=20 percent. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿全行程量測封面接觸與啟閉阻力並定位滲漏。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure seal contact and operating resistance throughout travel and locate leakage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：FreeSealThickness=30 mm; installedThickness=24 mm; compression=(30-24)/30*100=20 percent。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: FreeSealThickness=30 mm; installedThickness=24 mm; compression=(30-24)/30*100=20 percent. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「側封壓縮與摩擦」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Side-seal compression and friction\", which statement holds?","options":["曲面面積乘平均壓力必然就是垂直水壓力","原創教學假設：FreeSealThickness=30 mm; installedThickness=24 mm; compression=(30-24)/30*100=20 percent。","軸承反力不變就表示摩擦力矩永遠不變"],"optionsEn":["Curved area times mean pressure always equals vertical hydrostatic force","Original teaching assumptions: FreeSealThickness=30 mm; installedThickness=24 mm; compression=(30-24)/30*100=20 percent.","Constant bearing reaction guarantees constant friction torque"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：FreeSealThickness=30 mm; installedThickness=24 mm; compression=(30-24)/30*100=20 percent。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: FreeSealThickness=30 mm; installedThickness=24 mm; compression=(30-24)/30*100=20 percent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b250-v15-35","title":"側封壓縮與摩擦：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Side-seal compression and friction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「側封壓縮與摩擦」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Side-seal compression and friction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿全行程量測封面接觸與啟閉阻力並定位滲漏。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「偏斜門葉可使一側過壓縮而另一側失去密封」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure seal contact and operating resistance throughout travel and locate leakage. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A skewed gate can overcompress one seal while unloading the other. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以沿全行程量測封面接觸與啟閉阻力並定位滲漏作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對偏斜門葉可使一側過壓縮而另一側失去密封，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure seal contact and operating resistance throughout travel and locate leakage. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A skewed gate can overcompress one seal while unloading the other. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：偏斜門葉可使一側過壓縮而另一側失去密封。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A skewed gate can overcompress one seal while unloading the other. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿全行程量測封面接觸與啟閉阻力並定位滲漏。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「偏斜門葉可使一側過壓縮而另一側失去密封」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Measure seal contact and operating resistance throughout travel and locate leakage. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A skewed gate can overcompress one seal while unloading the other. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以沿全行程量測封面接觸與啟閉阻力並定位滲漏作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對偏斜門葉可使一側過壓縮而另一側失去密封，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure seal contact and operating resistance throughout travel and locate leakage. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A skewed gate can overcompress one seal while unloading the other. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「側封壓縮與摩擦」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Side-seal compression and friction\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","面板總面積相同就保證局部彎曲完全相同","沿全行程量測封面接觸與啟閉阻力並定位滲漏。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Equal total skin area guarantees identical local bending","Measure seal contact and operating resistance throughout travel and locate leakage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"沿全行程量測封面接觸與啟閉阻力並定位滲漏。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure seal contact and operating resistance throughout travel and locate leakage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b250-v15-36","title":"側封壓縮與摩擦：失效診斷","titleEn":"Side-seal compression and friction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「側封壓縮與摩擦」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Side-seal compression and friction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"偏斜門葉可使一側過壓縮而另一側失去密封。診斷時應採取以下查核：沿全行程量測封面接觸與啟閉阻力並定位滲漏，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A skewed gate can overcompress one seal while unloading the other. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure seal contact and operating resistance throughout travel and locate leakage. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「止水壓縮越多就必定越好且沒有代價」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"More seal compression is always better and has no adverse effect\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"偏斜門葉可使一側過壓縮而另一側失去密封。診斷時應採取以下查核：沿全行程量測封面接觸與啟閉阻力並定位滲漏，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"A skewed gate can overcompress one seal while unloading the other. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure seal contact and operating resistance throughout travel and locate leakage. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「側封壓縮與摩擦」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Side-seal compression and friction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["偏斜門葉可使一側過壓縮而另一側失去密封。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","兩側位置讀值相同就保證兩側荷載相同"],"optionsEn":["A skewed gate can overcompress one seal while unloading the other.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Equal side-position readings guarantee equal loads on both sides"],"answer":0,"explanation":"偏斜門葉可使一側過壓縮而另一側失去密封。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A skewed gate can overcompress one seal while unloading the other. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b250-v15-37","title":"同步行程與試運轉：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Synchronized travel and commissioning: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「同步行程與試運轉」如何影響大型弧形閘門安裝的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Synchronized travel and commissioning” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Large radial-gate installation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"雙側啟閉機不同步會造成門葉扭轉與封面不均，試運轉需逐工況核對行程、負荷與停留位置。兩側位移差除跨距僅是小角度扭斜指標；最終判定還需軸承、支臂與密封反應，不能只依位置訊號相近。 驗證時應同步記錄兩側行程與負荷並核對限位及停機後保持，並辨識以下失效情境：位置訊號一致但一側卡阻仍可能出現不均勻受力。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「同步行程與試運轉」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Unsynchronized drives skew the leaf and seals. Commissioning must compare travel, load and stopping positions across operating states. Differential travel divided by span is only a small-angle skew indicator; acceptance also requires bearing, arm and seal response rather than nearly equal position signals alone. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Record both travels and loads synchronously and check limits and position holding. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Matching position signals can coexist with unequal force when one side binds. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Synchronized travel and commissioning” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：LeftTravel=1250 mm; rightTravel=1244 mm; spacing=12000 mm; skewIndicator=(1250-1244)/12000=0.0005 rad。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: LeftTravel=1250 mm; rightTravel=1244 mm; spacing=12000 mm; skewIndicator=(1250-1244)/12000=0.0005 rad.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩側位置讀值相同就保證兩側荷載相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal side-position readings guarantee equal loads on both sides\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「同步行程與試運轉」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Synchronized travel and commissioning”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-37-k1","title":"同步行程與試運轉","titleEn":"Synchronized travel and commissioning","text":"雙側啟閉機不同步會造成門葉扭轉與封面不均，試運轉需逐工況核對行程、負荷與停留位置。兩側位移差除跨距僅是小角度扭斜指標；最終判定還需軸承、支臂與密封反應，不能只依位置訊號相近。","textEn":"Unsynchronized drives skew the leaf and seals. Commissioning must compare travel, load and stopping positions across operating states.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩側位置讀值相同就保證兩側荷載相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal side-position readings guarantee equal loads on both sides Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「同步行程與試運轉」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Synchronized travel and commissioning\" is correct?","options":["兩側位置讀值相同就保證兩側荷載相同","雙側啟閉機不同步會造成門葉扭轉與封面不均，試運轉需逐工況核對行程、負荷與停留位置。","理想弧門水壓通過鉸軸就代表全部荷載皆無力矩"],"optionsEn":["Equal side-position readings guarantee equal loads on both sides","Unsynchronized drives skew the leaf and seals.","Pressure passing through the trunnion means every gate load has zero moment"],"answer":1,"explanation":"雙側啟閉機不同步會造成門葉扭轉與封面不均，試運轉需逐工況核對行程、負荷與停留位置。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Unsynchronized drives skew the leaf and seals. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b250-v15-38","title":"同步行程與試運轉：定量估算","titleEn":"Synchronized travel and commissioning: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「同步行程與試運轉」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Synchronized travel and commissioning” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：LeftTravel=1250 mm; rightTravel=1244 mm; spacing=12000 mm; skewIndicator=(1250-1244)/12000=0.0005 rad。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: LeftTravel=1250 mm; rightTravel=1244 mm; spacing=12000 mm; skewIndicator=(1250-1244)/12000=0.0005 rad. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步記錄兩側行程與負荷並核對限位及停機後保持。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record both travels and loads synchronously and check limits and position holding.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：LeftTravel=1250 mm; rightTravel=1244 mm; spacing=12000 mm; skewIndicator=(1250-1244)/12000=0.0005 rad。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: LeftTravel=1250 mm; rightTravel=1244 mm; spacing=12000 mm; skewIndicator=(1250-1244)/12000=0.0005 rad. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「同步行程與試運轉」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Synchronized travel and commissioning\", which statement holds?","options":["兩鉸中心同高就保證三維軸線完全同軸","兩根吊索不論角度都各承受總重的一半","原創教學假設：LeftTravel=1250 mm; rightTravel=1244 mm; spacing=12000 mm; skewIndicator=(1250-1244)/12000=0.0005 rad。"],"optionsEn":["Equal trunnion-center elevations guarantee complete three-dimensional coaxiality","Two slings each carry half the weight regardless of angle","Original teaching assumptions: LeftTravel=1250 mm; rightTravel=1244 mm; spacing=12000 mm; skewIndicator=(1250-1244)/12000=0.0005 rad."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：LeftTravel=1250 mm; rightTravel=1244 mm; spacing=12000 mm; skewIndicator=(1250-1244)/12000=0.0005 rad。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: LeftTravel=1250 mm; rightTravel=1244 mm; spacing=12000 mm; skewIndicator=(1250-1244)/12000=0.0005 rad. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b250-v15-39","title":"同步行程與試運轉：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Synchronized travel and commissioning: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「同步行程與試運轉」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Synchronized travel and commissioning” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步記錄兩側行程與負荷並核對限位及停機後保持。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「位置訊號一致但一側卡阻仍可能出現不均勻受力」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record both travels and loads synchronously and check limits and position holding. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Matching position signals can coexist with unequal force when one side binds. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以同步記錄兩側行程與負荷並核對限位及停機後保持作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對位置訊號一致但一側卡阻仍可能出現不均勻受力，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Record both travels and loads synchronously and check limits and position holding. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Matching position signals can coexist with unequal force when one side binds. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：位置訊號一致但一側卡阻仍可能出現不均勻受力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Matching position signals can coexist with unequal force when one side binds. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步記錄兩側行程與負荷並核對限位及停機後保持。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「位置訊號一致但一側卡阻仍可能出現不均勻受力」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Record both travels and loads synchronously and check limits and position holding. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Matching position signals can coexist with unequal force when one side binds. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以同步記錄兩側行程與負荷並核對限位及停機後保持作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對位置訊號一致但一側卡阻仍可能出現不均勻受力，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Record both travels and loads synchronously and check limits and position holding. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Matching position signals can coexist with unequal force when one side binds. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「同步行程與試運轉」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Synchronized travel and commissioning\"?","options":["同步記錄兩側行程與負荷並核對限位及停機後保持。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","理想歐拉屈曲力就是現場支臂可直接承受荷載"],"optionsEn":["Record both travels and loads synchronously and check limits and position holding.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Ideal Euler load is the directly usable field capacity of the arm"],"answer":0,"explanation":"同步記錄兩側行程與負荷並核對限位及停機後保持。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record both travels and loads synchronously and check limits and position holding. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b250-v15-40","title":"同步行程與試運轉：失效診斷","titleEn":"Synchronized travel and commissioning: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b250-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「同步行程與試運轉」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Synchronized travel and commissioning” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"位置訊號一致但一側卡阻仍可能出現不均勻受力。診斷時應採取以下查核：同步記錄兩側行程與負荷並核對限位及停機後保持，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Matching position signals can coexist with unequal force when one side binds. Diagnose it by the following check: Record both travels and loads synchronously and check limits and position holding. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩側位置讀值相同就保證兩側荷載相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal side-position readings guarantee equal loads on both sides\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b250-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"位置訊號一致但一側卡阻仍可能出現不均勻受力。診斷時應採取以下查核：同步記錄兩側行程與負荷並核對限位及停機後保持，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Matching position signals can coexist with unequal force when one side binds. Diagnose it by the following check: Record both travels and loads synchronously and check limits and position holding. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b250-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「同步行程與試運轉」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Synchronized travel and commissioning\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","位置訊號一致但一側卡阻仍可能出現不均勻受力。","理想弧門水壓通過鉸軸就代表全部荷載皆無力矩"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Matching position signals can coexist with unequal force when one side binds.","Pressure passing through the trunnion means every gate load has zero moment"],"answer":1,"explanation":"位置訊號一致但一側卡阻仍可能出現不均勻受力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Matching position signals can coexist with unequal force when one side binds. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-radial","v15s-usace-hss","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
